    "body": "The xcframework build started failing in CI with:\r\n\r\n    mv: rename Sources/CashuDevKit/CashuDevKitFFI.h to \\\r\n        ../cdk/target/include/CashuDevKitFFI.h: No such file or directory\r\n\r\nRoot cause: in uniffi 0.30 library mode the per-crate uniffi.toml is not auto-discovered. The Swift module name comes from\r\ncrates/cdk-ffi/uniffi.toml (module_name = \"CashuDevKit\"). uniffi resolves which config to use by the crate's lib target name, but the cdk workspace now contains two crates whose lib target is named `cdk_ffi` (crates/cdk-ffi and bindings/kotlin/rust, the latter renamed from cdk_ffi_kotlin in cdk commit 9f6cd097). That collision makes the namespace lookup ambiguous, so module_name is dropped and bindgen emits cdk_ffiFFI.h instead of CashuDevKitFFI.h — and the subsequent `mv` fails.\r\n\r\nPassing --config explicitly pins the Swift bindings config regardless of the collision, restoring CashuDevKit* output. Applied to both build-xcframework.sh (cwd = cdk root) and generate-bindings.sh (cwd = cdk-ffi crate dir).",
